        OwnerDto dto = ownerMapper.toOwnerDto(owner);
        response.send(ResponseEntity.created(URI.create("/api/owners/" + owner.getId())).body(dto));
    }
}
```

`RespondWithOwner.java` (used by GET, which the test reads through) is the analogous read-back builder, also using `ownerMapper.toOwnerDto(owner)`.

Mapper: `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/mapper/OwnerMapper.java` — MapStruct `toOwnerDto(Owner)`. It maps many derived fields explicitly via `@Mapping` expressions; simple same-named fields like `bulkSignupWarning` are mapped by name automatically (no explicit `@Mapping`). A `capacityWarning` field on both `Owner` and `OwnerDto` would map automatically here.

